# Dotfiles are excluded by default and re-admitted one at a time, rather than
# listing what to hide. The inversion is deliberate: the failure mode here is a
# secret that was never named, and a default-deny list cannot forget one.
#
# .envrc.private holds every COLORS_PAR_* credential and is covered by the first
# line. So is .colors/, the rendered work directory — generated output, never
# source, and it carries resolved values from desired state.
.*
!.envrc
!.gitignore
!.nojekyll
!.agents
!.claude
node_modules/
